---
/**
 * PRIVACY POLICY — structured placeholder.
 *
 * IMPORTANT: this is a professionally structured template, NOT legal advice and
 * NOT a completed policy. South African processing is governed by POPIA (the
 * Protection of Personal Information Act 4 of 2013), which requires specific
 * disclosures and a designated Information Officer.
 *
 * Sections marked [TO CONFIRM] must be completed and the whole document
 * reviewed by a qualified legal advisor before launch.
 */
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "@components/ui/PageHero.astro";
import Section from "@components/ui/Section.astro";
import EditorialNote from "@components/ui/EditorialNote.astro";
import PendingValue from "@components/ui/PendingValue.astro";
import { company, isPublished } from "@data/company";

const addr = company.contact.address;
const updated = "Awaiting legal review";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Spartcon"
  description="How Spartcon (Pty) Ltd collects, uses and protects personal information submitted through this website."
  noindex
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    lead="How Spartcon (Pty) Ltd handles personal information submitted through this website."
  />

  <Section width="text">
    <EditorialNote title="This policy requires legal review before launch">
      <p>
        The structure below is complete and ready for content, but it is a
        template rather than a finished legal document. Processing of personal
        information in South Africa is governed by <strong>POPIA</strong> (the
        Protection of Personal Information Act 4 of 2013), which requires
        specific disclosures and a designated Information Officer.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sections marked <strong>[TO CONFIRM]</strong> need Spartcon's input, and
        the complete document should be reviewed by a qualified legal advisor
        before this page is published.
      </p>
    </EditorialNote>

    <div class="prose legal">
      <p class="legal__meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This website is operated by {company.legalName} ("Spartcon", "we", "us").
        {isPublished(addr) && (
          <>
            Our registered address is {addr.value.street}, {addr.value.suburb},{" "}
            {addr.value.city} {addr.value.postalCode}, {addr.value.province},{" "}
            {company.country}.
          </>
        )}
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Information Officer.</strong> POPIA requires every responsible
        party to designate an Information Officer and register them with the
        Information Regulator. <strong>[TO CONFIRM]</strong> — name and contact
        details of Spartcon's Information Officer.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you submit an enquiry through this website, we collect the
        information you provide in the form:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name</li>
        <li>Your company name, where provided</li>
        <li>Your email address</li>
        <li>Your telephone number</li>
        <li>The service you have selected</li>
        <li>The content of your message</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>[TO CONFIRM]</strong> — whether Spartcon uses website analytics,
        and if so which provider. This website currently loads no third-party
        analytics or advertising scripts. The contact page embeds a Google Maps
        frame, which is a third-party service subject to Google's own privacy
        terms.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Why we process it</h2>
      <p>
        We process the information you submit solely in order to respond to your
        enquiry and, where relevant, to provide a quotation or proposal and
        manage the resulting business relationship.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal information. We do not use it for marketing
        unrelated to your enquiry without your consent.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Legal basis</h2>
      <p>
        We process your information because it is necessary to respond to a
        request you have initiated, and in pursuit of our legitimate business
        interests as a construction and engineering service provider.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>[TO CONFIRM]</strong> — the operators and service providers
        Spartcon uses, which may include a website host, an email provider and a
        form-handling service. Each should be named here, together with whether
        any personal information is transferred outside South Africa.
      </p>

      <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>[TO CONFIRM]</strong> — Spartcon's retention period for enquiry
        records. POPIA requires that records not be retained for longer than is
        necessary for the purpose for which they were collected, unless another
        law requires retention.
      </p>

      <h2>7. How we protect it</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect
        personal information against loss, unauthorised access and unlawful
        processing. <strong>[TO CONFIRM]</strong> — a short description of the
        specific safeguards in place.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under POPIA you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Request access to the personal information we hold about you</li>
        <li>Request correction or deletion of that information</li>
        <li>Object to the processing of your information</li>
        <li>Lodge a complaint with the Information Regulator of South Africa</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise any of these rights, contact us using the details on our{" "}
        <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not set advertising or tracking cookies. Embedded
        third-party content, such as the Google Maps frame on the contact page,
        may set its own cookies when loaded. <strong>[TO CONFIRM]</strong> —
        whether any analytics cookies will be introduced, in which case a cookie
        notice and consent mechanism will be required.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of this
        page shows when it was last revised.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For any question about this policy or about how we handle your personal
        information:
      </p>
      <ul class="legal__contact">
        <li>
          <span>Email</span>
          <PendingValue field={company.contact.email} as="email" />
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>Telephone</span>
          <PendingValue field={company.contact.telephone} as="tel" />
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal__meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg-subtle);
    padding-bottom: var(--s-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    font-size: var(--t-h3);
    margin-top: var(--s-8);
  }

  .legal__contact {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: var(--s-4);
  }

  .legal__contact li {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .legal__contact span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-label);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg-subtle);
    min-width: 7rem;
  }
</style>
